  "retainedPreliminaryResults": {
    "reason": "Initial check found a snapshot field typo; the second found test-only private renderer access and incorrect preference-storage arguments. The final check compiled. First native release assertion used a stale published snapshot; the retained debugger proves all thirty renderer hold counts were zero. The cue regression caught omitted cue time/color descriptions, which now use the original cue description and help route. The manual was regenerated. Second focused qualification passed all fourteen then-existing feature checks. Subsequent review added fresh-key-only keyboard handling and normalized learned SP1 physical keys through manufacturer mode/deck-layer changes. The augmented keyboard block was initially placed in the wrong fixture; its retained third failure and final move remain recorded. Fourth qualification passed all fifteen feature checks plus native, accessibility, loop, scene and project regressions. Broad MIDI qualification found three legacy fixtures: one still expected the former direct HotCue command, and two repeated nonholding pad presses without physical releases. Final fixtures expect the shared captured command and send complete Note On/Off taps, preserving duplicate/held-key suppression in production. Fifth complete qualification passed 1957 checks and found one outdated saved-loop fixture asserting preset version 4 after the new version 5 schema. Final assertions use current preset 5/preferences 23 and verify version 4 saved-loop definitions retain their header and apply the same saved-loop bindings; older action injection refusal remains checked. A sixth compile was deliberately stopped before qualification when source review found the added compatibility assertion incorrectly expected decoding to rewrite an older portable header. The final fixture checks preserved version 4, identical bindings and the actual target application; the interrupted compile and frozen input hashes are retained. The seventh compile completed, but its first retention helper still named the fifth private executable and refused overwriting it. The corrected helper retained this newly compiled executable under its own seventh path before any qualification.",
